          "Treat the unopposed 2024 result as a vulnerability signal, not a vindication: without opposition data, you have no measure of whether discontent exists or could be mobilized; invest in year-round constituent feedback mechanisms and visible local presence to ensure that a challenger entering in a future cycle faces an incumbent with deep community relationships rather than the institutional inertia of an uncontested seat."
