          "Lead with economic security specificity — housing affordability, healthcare cost management, and wage growth — rather than abstract policy; the 25% renter rate and $75,638 income signal a constituency evaluating on whether government delivers tangible relief on their most acute financial concerns, not ideological positioning.",
          "Do not assume college education is a reliable Democratic marker in this district; at 20.5% college attainment, this is a mixed-education constituency where non-degreed professionals, tradespeople, and service-sector workers are the demographic majority, and many are swing voters whose allegiances follow economic outcomes rather than educational identity.",
          "Treat the 48% as a floor to defend actively, not a result to manage passively; in a suburban Indianapolis district this evenly divided, a shift of three to four percentage points in voter preference or turnout among renters, younger adults, or working-class homeowners facing inflation is sufficient to flip the seat to Republican control in the next cycle."
