          { name: "Treating the Low College Attainment (15.2%) as Evidence of Low Political Engagement or Limited Sophistication", tag: "avoid", why: "Low college attainment correlates with working-class employment and renters, not with political disengagement or vulnerability to simplistic messaging; it correlates with material economic concerns and skepticism of government that fails to deliver on those concerns. A representative who talks down to a working-class, non-college-educated constituency or who assumes they will respond to abstract conservative rhetoric rather than to concrete economic policy attention will find that constituency receptive to an alternative. This is a constituency that evaluates on results, not on partisan identity, and a legislative record that demonstrates attention to their material concerns is the only durable foundation for political support." }
