          "Understand specifically what the 3.34% demographic gap represents and why it voted 76-24 against Republican: whether immigrant families, younger professionals relocating in, or other communities, this group's presence in a wealthy, college-educated district is a data point about demographic change that demands specific strategic attention rather than dismissal as noise.",
          "Engage college-educated voters on governance competence and local quality-of-life delivery, not abstract ideology: at 27.2% college attainment and $87K median income, this constituency evaluates on whether schools are excellent, infrastructure is maintained, and local government functions efficiently — not on partisan positioning alone.",
          "Do not treat 76% as a floor or assume the seat is durable without active constituent engagement: in a district this prosperous and settled, complacency by an incumbent or overconfidence that demographic stability equals electoral durability is the most common path to unexpected vulnerability."
