          "Build active relationship with the ~5.79% AIAN gap population: this is a smaller swing constituency than in other districts, but in a 52-48 race, understanding whether Native American voters in this district are mobilized or persuadable is essential. Early engagement around tribal priorities prevents the opposition from capturing this bloc by default.",
          "Consolidate younger-adult support through workforce development and wage policy: the 39.5 median age and 22.7% college attainment signal a constituency that values economic mobility pathways and actual wage growth over educational credential expansion. Legislative focus on apprenticeship programs, wage standards, and sector-specific training is more directly resonant than traditional education rhetoric.",
          "Do not treat 52% as a majority — treat it as a mandate to prove Democratic governance delivers for this specific constituency: at 48% opposition in a working-class renter district, Chesser is one cycle of legislative underperformance away from losing to a Republican who better diagnoses what working people in HD-71 actually need."
