          "Build educational and workforce pipeline initiatives that address the 14.9% college attainment ceiling: community college affordability, apprenticeship programs, trade credential pathways, and employer partnerships that create economic mobility for the 85% of adults without a four-year degree are the practical mechanisms for improving long-term household income in this constituency.",
          "Maintain active, differentiated engagement across the Black (27%), Hispanic (19%), Asian (11%), and other minority constituencies — avoid absorbing them into an undifferentiated 'coalition narrative' and instead address specific economic and healthcare concerns that vary by community (workforce representation in public contracting, immigration policy clarity for Hispanic and Asian constituents, healthcare access for Black and other communities).",
          "Recognize that an unopposed 2024 victory provides no data about whether opposition exists or how deep constituent loyalty actually runs — treat the seat as competitive in the next cycle and build durable constituent relationships around specific economic deliverables rather than assuming demographic trend or partisan registration will hold the seat indefinitely."
