          { name: "Racial equity and criminal justice reform narratives", tag: "avoid", why: "Black/African American residents represent only 1.28% of the district. Candidates advocating for broad racial equity initiatives or criminal justice reform without strong local crime data or community demand risk appearing disconnected from constituent priorities and may activate unnecessary opposition. A 72% winning margin suggests the electorate is not primed for these debates and messaging here is strategically inefficient." }
