          "Emphasize rural and agricultural economic resilience—farm support, rural broadband, small-business tax relief—without college-subsidy or large-scale immigration rhetoric that signals disconnect from district economic roots.",
          "Avoid identity-politics or racial equity framing: the district is 87% White with minimal Black/Latino populations, and a 72% margin means no competitive pressure to activate these debates. Silence is safer than signaling.",
          "Position K-12 education around vocational pathways and local accountability, not higher-ed expansion; 79.4% of adults lack college degrees, and tuition-forward messaging will land as elitist in this constituency."
