          "Champion skilled trades and non-degree pathways as equally dignified to college credentials: 75.8% of adults lack a BA, so vocational and apprenticeship framing is not a niche—it is the baseline economic reality and a values anchor.",
          "Engage Hispanic/Latino voters (8.71%) on economic opportunity and community belonging, not demographic narrative: avoid both dismissiveness and over-reactive emphasis on racial categories; focus on jobs, small business, and inclusion.",
          "Avoid abstract culture-war or credentialism frames: the unopposed result masks vulnerability if messaging drifts from material household economics to identity signaling or college-centric values; an opponent has room to reposition."
