          { name: "Generic Partisan Messaging in a Suburban Professional District", tag: "avoid", why: "College-educated suburban professionals evaluate on competence, specific policy outcomes, and whether representation is delivering material benefits—not abstract conservative or liberal positioning. An incumbent or challenger who relies on partisan rhetoric without grounding in specific governance accomplishments or clear policy proposals will lose persuasive power with the 38.6% college-educated plurality who expect their representative to engage substantively. This demographic will hold representatives accountable on actual performance, not party affiliation." }
