          "Lead any opposition challenge with homeowner economic concerns: property tax fairness, school funding adequacy, water quality and infrastructure, and local government accountability are the material issues for a 70.8%-homeowner, $73,364-income constituency that evaluates on whether state government is delivering tangible benefits.",
          "Engage the ~5.5% demographic gap and minority communities with specific constituent attention: Hispanic, Black, and Asian residents in IN-SD-16 may be underrepresented in turnout, undertargetted by opposition campaigns, or genuinely satisfied with incumbent performance — but their actual concerns around economic mobility, education quality, and healthcare access deserve direct engagement rather than assumption.",
          "Recognize that unopposed status is a vulnerability as much as a strength: an incumbent with no recent electoral competition may lack the organizational muscle and message discipline necessary to defend against a well-resourced challenger, and may have become complacent about constituent service — making this seat more vulnerable than the 2024 result alone suggests."
