          "Lead with renter economic security and housing affordability: at 37.3% renters and $62,297 income, the district's majority renters are evaluating candidates on whether rents are rising faster than wages, whether there is affordable housing stock, and whether the incumbent understands the difference between homeowner and renter interests. Make housing policy and renter protections a signature constituent issue rather than an afterthought.",
