          "Build specific constituent relationships with the ~3.4% demographic gap (likely AIAN residents) and the 9.21% Hispanic and 7.92% Asian communities: in a high-income suburban district, these constituencies' economic mobility, education access, and healthcare equity concerns can become invisible if the dominant narrative centers only on the Anglo professional majority. Targeted constituent engagement here can both improve governance and recover persuadable voters."
