          "Make housing affordability and renter-focused policy central to your governance message: with 50.1% renters at a $70,884 median income, tenant protections, inclusionary zoning, and support for first-time homebuyers are not peripheral issues — they are core constituent concerns for half the district.",
          "Maintain constituent service responsiveness and visible community presence as a baseline expectation, not a competitive advantage — unopposed status is not a signal that you can reduce engagement; it is an invitation to discover in a competitive cycle whether the loyalty was ever as solid as the vote total suggested."
