          { name: "Assuming the Unopposed Result Reflects a Durable Supermajority", tag: "avoid", why: "The 100% partisan result is an artifact of no opposition, not evidence that IN-SD-38 is a supermajority-Republican district in working-class demographics or voter behavior. An incumbent who campaigns as though this seat is safe and requires only base mobilization will be vulnerable to a challenger who speaks directly to the working-family economic concerns that a $54,660-income, 33.5% renter constituency faces in rising-cost environments. The absence of 2022 opposition should trigger greater strategic urgency, not greater complacency." },
          { name: "Neglecting Working-Class Messaging in Favor of Ideological Conservative Positioning", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where median income is $54,660, childcare and healthcare costs are likely consuming a substantial share of household budgets, and rent represents a significant housing cost for one-third of residents, messaging that emphasizes abstract conservative ideology rather than concrete policy responses to working-family economic concerns will fail to mobilize the incumbent's base and leave an opening for a challenger who speaks to material needs. The incumbent's message must connect state policy to the lived experience of working families in IN-SD-38, or risk finding that 100% opposition in a future contested race is far more possible than the unopposed 2022 result suggested." }
