          "Lead with homeowner economic security and municipal service delivery: property tax management, school funding and quality, police and fire service reliability, and infrastructure maintenance are the direct governance concerns for an 84% white, 73% homeowner, $74,740-income constituency. Demonstrate consistent delivery on these material issues through budget prioritization and legislative record.",
          "Engage the renter and non-white communities with specific policy attention to their distinct concerns—affordable housing access, workforce training and economic mobility, equitable school resources, and healthcare access in an underserved population. This is not tokenism; these constituencies represent real constituent needs and future electoral risk if ignored.",
          "Build relationships with employers and economic development institutions that retain and attract workers to the district: manufacturing, logistics, healthcare, education sectors where residents actually work. A legislator who understands the district's employment ecosystem and actively advocates for workforce development and employer partnership is addressing the economic security that underpins homeowner confidence."
